{
  "$schema": "./SCHEMA.md#node-request",
  "description": "Node-to-node request credential (avalon_protocol::node_request::verify_node_request_header). A node signs one HTTP request with its Ed25519 key over avalon-node-request-v1, then u32-BE length-prefixed method, path (no query), sha256 of the body, network id, recipient and signer peer id, then timestamp as unix seconds big-endian i64, then the 16 nonce bytes. The credential travels in the x-avalon-node-auth header as 'v1; peer=<peer id>; key=<64 lowercase hex>; ts=<decimal unix seconds>; nonce=<32 lowercase hex>; sig=<128 lowercase hex>', parsed strictly: exactly those fields in that order separated by '; ', ASCII, at most 512 bytes, no leading-zero or signed timestamp, peer id [A-Za-z0-9]{1,128}. The recipient and network are not in the header: the verifier tries each of its accepted recipients, so a signature for another recipient or network is reported as bad_signature. Order of checks: header form, request field validity (uppercase method, path starting with '/' and without '?' or '#', bounded lengths), timestamp window (inclusive, either direction), public key, signature (strict Ed25519). expected.error is one of malformed, invalid_request, invalid_key, stale, future, bad_signature, or null when accepted. Vectors with signingRecipient also carry messageHex, the exact signed message. The caller still derives the peer id from the key and rejects repeated nonces; neither is covered here. signerPeerId is a fixed placeholder string, not a real libp2p id.",
  "notSupported": {
    "csharp": "the C# SDK has no node-request signing or verification: the credential is for node-to-node routes that are not in the server's OpenAPI document, so no SDK client calls them.",
    "rust": "the Rust SDK has no node-request signing or verification: the credential is for node-to-node routes that are not in the server's OpenAPI document, so no SDK client calls them.",
    "typescript": "the TypeScript SDK has no node-request signing or verification: the credential is for node-to-node routes that are not in the server's OpenAPI document, so no SDK client calls them."
  },
